    <statement><p>For the function <m>f(x)=5 e^{x}</m> and <m>g(x)=x^{9}</m>, find the following:</p>
<p><alert>(a)</alert> 
<m>f(g(1))</m>= <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><alert>(b)</alert> 
<m>g(f(1))</m>= <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p><alert>(c)</alert> 
<m>f(g(x))</m>= <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
<p><alert>(d)</alert> 
<m>g(f(x))</m>= <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0004"/></p>
<p><alert>(e)</alert> 
<m>f(t)g(t)</m>= <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0005"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>5e</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left(5e\right)^{9}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>5e^{x^{9}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left(5e^{x}\right)^{9}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>5e^{t}t^{9}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><alert>(a)</alert>
<m>f(g(1))=f(1^{9})=5 e^{(1^{9})}</m>



<alert>(b)</alert>
<m>g(f(1))=g(5 e^{1})=(5 e^{1})^{9}</m>



<alert>(c)</alert>
<m>f(g(x))=f(x^{9})=5 e^{(x^{9})}</m>



<alert>(d)</alert>
<m>g(f(x))=g(5 e^{x})=(5 e^{x})^{9}</m>



<alert>(e)</alert>
<m>f(t)g(t)=5 e^{t} t^{9}</m>



</solution>
